# Profiles are one workspace's project facts — never shared library content.
#
# The library master ships `profiles/` empty by design: a profile filled in for one
# project reads as a *decision* in every other project that inherits it, which is the
# exact drift the library exists to prevent (see profiles/README.md).
#
# Each adopting workspace fills its own profiles in locally. They stay untracked here
# so a `git pull` of a library update never clobbers them and a `git push` never
# publishes one project's session tiers, env tables, ids, or thresholds to another.
profiles/*
!profiles/README.md
